      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yankee_Lake%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was originally called Lingamore Lake before the creek was dammed to create the lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yankee_Lake%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1928 Ernest Houston Stewart and John Jurko opened a dance hall that drew big‑band stars like Glenn Miller.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
